{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg3Q19XjUFDZECRzUjSyC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01H22ryJPXXAEDHpRBYjEjKU","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='AGENTS.md'\ns=open(p).read()\nanchor=\"`test/hydration.ts` imports `state.ts` and `scaffold.ts` from source alongside the built app.\\n\"\nassert anchor in s\nadd=anchor+\"\"\"`test/hydration.ts` also scans every JS asset under `build/client`\nfor `ISOLATION_MARKERS`: fixed strings that must not ship, each first\nproven present in a control file (`build/server/app.js`, or\n`dist/build.js` for the transform, which the example's server build\ndoes not contain). Markers must come from stripped code only, never\nfrom Badge/Notice markup or text they share; when Counter's markup\nchanges, update its marker in the same commit.\n\"\"\"\ns=s.replace(anchor,add)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngit add AGENTS.md && git commit -qm \"docs: note the isolation markers in AGENTS.md\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\"\nmkdir -p .nightralph && cat > .nightralph/notes.md <<'EOF'\n# 09 built-asset isolation check -- notes\n\nThe blocker (example build) is resolved at HEAD: `npm run build:hydration`\nsucceeds (vite.config.ts now imports ../dist/vite.js).\n\nImplemented in test/hydration.ts: ISOLATION_MARKERS table, jsAssets()\nrecursive scan of build/client and build/server, a test that both scans\nfound files, one test per marker (positive control first, then one\nassertion per client JS file), and an inverse test that\n`class=\"badge-text\"` (Badge, kept) is found in a client asset.\n\nMarkers:\n1. Counter: `aria-label=\"Decrement\"` (in build/server/app.js only).\n2. Scaffold: `<!--microtags:main-->` (in build/server/app.js; also in the\n   client index.html, which is not JS and is not scanned -- the spec says\n   JS assets).\n3. Build entry: `microtags/build requires \"typescript\"`. Interpretation:\n   no file under example-hydration/build/server contains src/build.ts, so\n   the control file is dist/build.js (built by build:node, which\n   build:hydration runs first). Documented in a table comment.\n\nVerified during development (not committed): a bogus marker failed with\n\"BOGUS marker is stale: not found in example-hydration/build/server/app.js\",\nand a marker present in the client (`notice-text`) failed the per-file\n\"lacks\" assertion. The per-file loop is skipped when the control fails.\n\nRunning hydration test standalone needs `npm run build` first (dist/htm.js).\nLint requires example-hydration/build removed.\nEOF\necho ok"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":229,"cache_read_input_tokens":69076,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":229},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"56a21c49-f68c-48e2-bb47-2c4bbcde85a7","uuid":"96815b71-fc0f-4544-98eb-9fef909675b7","timestamp":"2026-10-15T04:32:53.982Z","request_id":"req_011Cg3Q19E8dqeUXU9PCuKfj","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01H22ryJPXXAEDHpRBYjEjKU":{"command":"cd /Users/nick/code/microtags.millitags-lessons-09-built-asset-isolation-check && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='AGENTS.md'\ns=open(p).read()\nanchor=\"`test/hydration.ts` imports `state.ts` and `scaffold.ts` from source alongside the built app.\\n\"\nassert anchor in s\nadd=anchor+\"\"\"`test/hydration.ts` also scans every JS asset under `build/client`\nfor `ISOLATION_MARKERS`: fixed strings that must not ship, each first\nproven present in a control file (`build/server/app.js`, or\n`dist/build.js` for the transform, which the example's server build\ndoes not contain). Markers must come from stripped code only, never\nfrom Badge/Notice markup or text they share; when Counter's markup\nchanges, update its marker in the same commit.\n\"\"\"\ns=s.replace(anchor,add)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngit add AGENTS.md && git commit -qm \"docs: note the isolation markers in AGENTS.md\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\"\nmkdir -p .nightralph && cat > .nightralph/notes.md <<'EOF'\n# 09 built-asset isolation check -- notes\n\nThe blocker (example build) is resolved at HEAD: `npm run build:hydration`\nsucceeds (vite.config.ts now imports ../dist/vite.js).\n\nImplemented in test/hydration.ts: ISOLATION_MARKERS table, jsAssets()\nrecursive scan of build/client and build/server, a test that both scans\nfound files, one test per marker (positive control first, then one\nassertion per client JS file), and an inverse test that\n`class=\"badge-text\"` (Badge, kept) is found in a client asset.\n\nMarkers:\n1. Counter: `aria-label=\"Decrement\"` (in build/server/app.js only).\n2. Scaffold: `<!--microtags:main-->` (in build/server/app.js; also in the\n   client index.html, which is not JS and is not scanned -- the spec says\n   JS assets).\n3. Build entry: `microtags/build requires \"typescript\"`. Interpretation:\n   no file under example-hydration/build/server contains src/build.ts, so\n   the control file is dist/build.js (built by build:node, which\n   build:hydration runs first). Documented in a table comment.\n\nVerified during development (not committed): a bogus marker failed with\n\"BOGUS marker is stale: not found in example-hydration/build/server/app.js\",\nand a marker present in the client (`notice-text`) failed the per-file\n\"lacks\" assertion. The per-file loop is skipped when the control fails.\n\nRunning hydration test standalone needs `npm run build` first (dist/htm.js).\nLint requires example-hydration/build removed.\nEOF\necho ok"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_01H22ryJPXXAEDHpRBYjEjKU":{"cwd":"/Users/nick/code/microtags.millitags-lessons-09-built-asset-isolation-check"}}}
